m, Inc. and changed its name to Zevra Therapeutics, Inc. in February 2023. The company was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Neil F. McFarlane | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 61 people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $207K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Zevra Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $540M market cap on $106M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +117% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -256% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $2M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +29.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +29.8% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the 